cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, the SynB2B-Fraud-Stream extension, or its results, please cite the software entry below."
title: "synb2b-fraud-stream: budget-constrained conformal risk control for fraud decisioning under drift and endogenous label arrival"
abstract: >-
  A selective-decision layer that wraps any fraud scorer: it controls the residual
  fraud rate on auto-allowed transactions, respects a hard analyst review budget, and
  stays auditable while the data drifts. The repository also publishes
  SynB2B-Fraud-Stream, two additive annotation layers over the SynB2B-Fraud benchmark
  - a three-event drift schedule with distinct covariate, concept and prior
  mechanisms, and an endogenous label-arrival model in which the policy's own action
  determines whether, when, and how truthfully each transaction is ever labelled.
